(text "HAND-WHEEL INDEX SENSOR (one magnet, one pulse per stitch)" (at 200.66 210.82 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid eda87660-5db8-41b8-91f0-aa10fb9f0abf))
(text "HAND-WHEEL ENCODER (two Hall latches, quadrature; same cable as the index)" (at 297.18 160.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 2b987a64-e8e5-43e6-b82c-259204522c7b))
(text "HEEL SWITCH" (at 55.88 199.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6d1e2165-7171-44c3-a7a5-44c19c76acc3))
(text "SWITCHES (internal pull-ups)" (at 170.18 218.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 3e6ec101-fcbc-4a82-8113-01b635f7ef62))
(text "OPERATOR INPUTS (RC-filtered ADC)" (at 20.32 139.7 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 34af2032-6c92-40d6-8a9c-7a29d5bf6885))
(text "NOTES. A concept drawn by Claude at Bob Drzyzgula's direction, October 2026: not built, not tested, values not checked." (at 20.32 258.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 0167eb3c-5a47-438e-a6cc-d0bd6d2d6adb))
(text "1. After Freescale AN1662: zero-cross interrupt sets a timer alarm (or a PIO program); at the firing delay a ~100 us gate pulse fires the" (at 20.32 261.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 33c867da-c283-47c7-95ac-3932c748f555))
(text "   triac; hand-wheel period from edge timestamps; speed loop every half-cycle (120 Hz); stall watchdog. Added: isolation, relay, inputs." (at 20.32 263.40000000000003 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid eca8693b-d1c8-49e1-aa60-ed974ea36249))
(text "2. Pins (RP2350B): FIRE GP4; RELAY GP5; ZC GP6; HALL (index) GP7; ENC_A/B GP2/GP3 (PIO counter); STITCH GP10; HEEL GP11; NEEDLE GP12;" (at 20.32 265.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 64bbf8ef-56cc-49ec-864d-28177d50ddba))
(text "   knee, pedal, FSR, limit on ADC0-3 (GP40-43); ISENSE ADC4; ADC5-7 spare; GP8/GP9 UART1 for debug (or USB serial). Avoid GP0, GP23, GP25 (PSRAM, key, LED)." (at 20.32 268.20000000000005 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 97a629ae-ee7c-40f6-8c58-5609186e214a))
(text "3. PS1 feeds VSYS through D2, so USB may stay plugged in (the control side is SELV). Flash by UF2 (BOOTSEL) or SWD. Drive GP4 at 8-12 mA." (at 20.32 270.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid a0736b2e-ac2d-4c38-9699-65ce190a48da))
(text "4. Fire only after a zero-cross has been seen and the command is zero; close K1 last and open it first. Never scope the line side." (at 20.32 273.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6521331d-dd2d-4069-a617-ff934bab82c7))
(text "5. R7/R8: ~3.9 mA peak in the H11AA1; R11: ~8 mA into U3 from 3.3 V; R6/C2 fitted only if a snubberless triac false-fires. T1 optional: motor lead through its window, 0.1 V/A about 1.65 V." (at 20.32 275.40000000000003 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 360c97d4-7953-4765-ade2-d7eb84cd68ea))
(text "6. On a WeAct RP2350B Core board, feed PS1 to the 5V pin: the board has its own diode from USB VBUS, so D2 may be left out." (at 20.32 277.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 43c6320e-9596-4369-b3d3-7b521cad4776))
(text "7. Heel: momentary switch to GND in either pedal (J5 pin 4, J6 pin 3); a heel tap sends the needle to its other stop." (at 20.32 280.20000000000005 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 9791bf36-26bd-4321-9614-24b58321ded2))
